# Customer Behavior & Segmentation Analysis (Excel)

## Overview
An Excel dashboard that analyzes 5,630 e-commerce customers to understand behavior, satisfaction and churn, supported by a report on customer segmentation methods.

## Dataset
- 5,630 unique customers, 20 attributes
- Key fields: Churn, Tenure, PreferredLoginDevice, CityTier, PreferredPaymentMode, Gender, MaritalStatus, HourSpendOnApp, SatisfactionScore, Complain, OrderCount, DaySinceLastOrder, CashbackAmount
- The workbook includes a Data Dict sheet describing each field

## What is in the workbook
- Data: the customer dataset, with VLOOKUP and INDEX-MATCH helper columns
- Pivot tables: 9 PivotTables (for example average tenure by city tier, satisfaction and churn, payment mode counts, complaints, cashback and days since last order)
- Dashboard: 10 charts and 2 slicers

## Quick facts from the data
- Churned customers: 948 of 5,630 (16.8%)
- Customers who complained: 28.5%
- Churn rate: 31.7% for customers who complained vs 10.9% for those who did not

## Report
A 10-page report explains four customer segmentation methods (demographic, behavioral, value-based, lifecycle), the RFM model and recommended next steps for marketing and retention.

## Notes and limits
- The dataset has recency (DaySinceLastOrder) and frequency (OrderCount) fields but no order value, so a full RFM score is not calculated here.
- Some fields contain missing values.

## Files
- customer segmentation data analysis.xlsx: workbook with data, pivot tables and dashboard
- customer segmentation dashboard.png: dashboard preview
- Customer-Segmentation-Report-final.pdf: segmentation report

